1
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
We had twenty years to prepare. So did they.

2
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Independence Day: Resurgence is a action, adventure, science
fiction film directed by Roland Emmerich.

3
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:30,000
We always knew they were coming back.

4
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Using recovered alien technology, the nations of Earth have
collaborated on an immense defense program to protect the planet.

5
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
But nothing can prepare us for the aliens’ advanced and unprecedented force.

6
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Only the ingenuity of a few brave men and women can bring
our world back from the brink of extinction.

7
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:42,000
Jake Morrison, played by Liam Hemsworth.

8
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
David Levinson, played by Jeff Goldblum.

9
00:43:12,000 --> 00:43:18,000
Dylan Hiller, played by Jessie T. Usher.

10
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
President Whitmore, played by Bill Pullman.

11
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
Patricia Whitmore, played by Maika Monroe.

12
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
Charlie Miller, played by Travis Tope.

13
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
Independence Day: Resurgence is a 2016 American science fiction action film co-written, directed, and co-produced by Roland
Emmerich and co-written and co-produced by Dean Devlin, serving as a standalone sequel to Independence Day (1996).

14
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
It stars an ensemble cast that consists of Liam Hemsworth, Jeff
Goldblum, Bill Pullman, Maika Monroe, Jessie T.

15
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Usher, Travis Tope, William Fichtner, Charlotte Gainsbourg, and Judd Hirsch.

16
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
The film takes place twenty years after the events of the first film, during which the United Nations has
collaborated to form the Earth Space Defense, an international military defense and research organization.

17
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Through reverse engineering, the world has fused the power of alien technology
with humanity's and laid the groundwork to resist a second invasion.

18
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:30,000
Plans for a sequel to Independence Day began as early as 2001, with 20th
Century Fox eventually green-lighting the project in 2014.

19
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:18,000
Principal photography began in April 2015 at locations primarily in New Mexico but also in
the Bonneville Salt Flats of Utah, which were featured in the original.

20
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
This was one of Robert Loggia's final projects before he died, and the film is
dedicated in memory of him and he is commemorated during its closing credits.

21
01:40:48,000 --> 01:40:54,000
Independence Day: Resurgence was released by 20th Century Fox in the United States on June 24,
2016, twenty years after the release of Independence Day, in 2D, 3D, and IMAX 3D.

22
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:42,000
It received largely negative reviews from critics and audiences who felt the film lacked the hype of the original and was a
financial disappointment, grossing $389.7 million worldwide at the box office against its $165 million budget.

23
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
Following the film's release, director Emmerich openly expressed his dissatisfaction with the completed film, as he
regretted making it without Will Smith's involvement (Smith was one of the central protagonists in the first film).

24
01:55:12,000 --> 01:55:18,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
